## description of what was run, for what purpose
Modal GPU run of `modal_gguf_vlm_export.py::run` to validate GGUF export for `unsloth/llava-1.5-7b-hf` after allowing CLIP vision encoders in converter.
- Environment: Modal A10G, torch 2.5.1+cu121, unsloth editable branch `gguf-vision-export`, unsloth_zoo==2025.11.5.
- Actions: merged to 16-bit, patched converter (qwen2 vocab + Llava clip vision), converted text + mmproj to GGUF, quantized text to q8_0.
- Outputs: `llava-1.5-7b-hf.Q8_0.gguf` (~6.7 GB) and `llava-1.5-7b-hf.BF16-mmproj.gguf` (~622 MB) produced successfully.
- Notes: same non-blocking warnings about missing `triton_kernels` and `causal_conv1d`; conversion succeeded end-to-end.

## description of what was run, for what purpose
Modal GPU attempt for `liuhaotian/llava-v1.6-mistral-7b` to broaden VLM coverage.
- Outcome: Failed early because transformers==4.57.2 in the modal image does not support `model_type=llava_mistral`; FastVisionModel aborted before conversion even with trust_remote_code=True. No artifacts produced.
- Action left: rerun with newer transformers when modal base image is updated or pin a supported llava-v1.6 fork.

## description of what was run, for what purpose
Modal image rebuild attempt to upgrade transformers to 4.50.2 for llava-v1.6 support.
- Outcome: Build failed at pip resolution because `unsloth_zoo==2025.11.5` pins transformers <=4.57.2 and >=4.51.3; requested 4.50.2 is out of range. Image not built; no run executed.
- Action left: would require an unsloth_zoo release that supports newer transformers or a custom fork; otherwise llava-v1.6 remains unsupported in this environment.

## description of what was run, for what purpose
Modal GPU run of `modal_gguf_vlm_export.py::run` for `Qwen/Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct` to extend coverage to a larger Qwen2-VL model.
- Environment: Modal A10G, torch 2.5.1+cu121, unsloth editable branch `gguf-vision-export`, unsloth_zoo==2025.11.5.
- Actions: merged to 16-bit, patched converter (qwen2 vocab + clip-vision allowance), converted text + mmproj to GGUF, quantized text to q8_0.
- Outputs: `Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct.Q8_0.gguf` (~7.54 GB) and `Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct.BF16-mmproj.gguf` (vision projector) produced successfully.
- Notes: same benign warnings about missing `triton_kernels` and `causal_conv1d`; conversion finished end-to-end.

## description of what was run, for what purpose
Modal GPU attempt of `modal_gguf_vlm_export.py::run` for `Qwen/Qwen-VL` (original Qwen-VL) to validate GGUF export after adding VLM patches.
- Environment: Modal A10G, torch 2.5.1+cu121, unsloth editable (with gguf_vlm_helpers + BeamSearchScorer alias), unsloth_zoo==2025.11.5.
- Outcome: Downloaded config and Python modules; failed early because `transformers_stream_generator` imported `BeamSearchScorer` from transformers top-level (missing in 4.57.2). Run aborted before weight loading (app ap-cc6PqO99oR187yCUUa2Sgp).
- Action item: provide BeamSearchScorer alias; rerun.

## description of what was run, for what purpose
Modal GPU re-attempt for `Qwen/Qwen-VL` after adding BeamSearchScorer alias in `unsloth/models/vision.py`.
- Environment: Modal A10G, torch 2.5.1+cu121, unsloth editable (BeamSearchScorer alias), unsloth_zoo==2025.11.5.
- Outcome: Model download proceeded; load failed when transformers enforced torch>=2.6 for loading PyTorch `.bin` shards (CVE-2025-32434 safeguard) with torch 2.5.1. No GGUF artifacts produced (app ap-vLy60C02VeUOj8KCABUPbS).
- Action left: either upgrade modal image to torch>=2.6-compatible stack or locate a safetensors variant of Qwen-VL; current image pinned to torch 2.5.1 for other successful runs.
